{"chunk_id": "72c40ade6462", "text": "Bhishma recounts teachings of the sage Parasara to King Janaka about death, rebirth, and the path to liberation. The passage first explains how the body, a temporary compound of impure elements driven by past desires, dissolves and reforms according to karma. After death the soul (jiva) wanders before taking another body, its destiny shaped by past acts. Ignorance is described as humanity\u2019s single true enemy, overcome only by wisdom. Human birth is praised as a rare opportunity for righteous action, compassion, and spiritual discipline. In the dialogue, Parasara teaches that detachment is the root of good, knowledge the highest path, and non\u2011violence the greatest gift. Through renunciation, disciplined living, and insight into the soul\u2019s nature, one may escape the cycle of birth and death and attain lasting happiness.\nParasara teaches Janaka that detachment, knowledge, righteous action, and control of the mind lead to liberation beyond the cycle of birth and death.\nThemes: detachment, karma and rebirth, knowledge and yoga, renunciation vs sensuality, ignorance as the true enemy", "vector": [0.008139637298882008, 0.011838278733193874, 0.009341860190033913, -0.0031730791088193655, -0.0168442539870739, 0.001224394654855132, -0.017777126282453537, -0.018026767298579216, -0.04351651296019554, -0.017763987183570862, 0.023164134472608566, 0.027959885075688362, 0.006333019118756056, 0.032374605536460876, 0.008566656149923801, -0.007975399494171143, 0.04956047236919403, -0.01392738614231348, 0.03602725639939308, -0.01421644538640976, 0.00515379011631012, -0.00310245668515563, 0.003017053008079529, 0.006773177068680525, -0.002747702645137906, 0.02112758159637451, 0.02856428176164627, -0.01990565098822117, 0.0016062480863183737, -0.030403748154640198, -0.006773177068680525, 0.000656541611533612, -0.019117308780550957, -0.007719188462942839, -0.038260895758867264, 0.0016982214292511344, -0.011582067236304283, -0.00135332148